/* ItemDatabase (Armory) stylesheet TEMPLATE — rendered by
   core.theme.build_qss_from() through ItemDatabase/app.py's
   _load_qss_text(), once per theme.  `{token}` is a MASTER §2 semantic
   token, `{data.<kind>.<key>}` a MASTER §4-4 data colour, and
   `{token|alpha}` that colour at a given alpha (see core/theme.py's
   _PLACEHOLDER_RE for why the alpha form exists).  This block spells
   placeholders with SINGLE braces: a real double-brace one written in a comment is
   still substituted (the renderer reads the whole file), and an example
   token name is not a token.

   WHY THIS FILE IS NOT SCOPED.  The application sheet prefixes every rule
   with `QWidget[aion2="true"]` so it cannot reach in here
   (tests/test_app_sheet_isolation.py).  The Armory's windows are
   parentless, own this sheet outright (window.setStyleSheet), and nothing
   else in the process ever receives it — so a scope here would only be a
   prefix with nothing on the other side of it.

   NEAREST-TOKEN MAP.  The hand-written ancestor of this file (1,205 lines,
   190 selectors, "Abyss, copied intentionally") predates the token system,
   so most of its values are near a token rather than on one.  Every
   substitution that was NOT exact is listed here; everything not listed
   rendered byte-identical for Abyss.

     legacy value                     token                      why
     ------------------------------   ------------------------   ---------------------------------
     white                            {fg}                     MASTER §2: text is slate.100, never pure white
     #e2e8f0 #e6ecf5 #e7ebf3          {fg}                     three spellings of "the main text colour"
     #cbd5e1                          {fg.secondary}           slate.300
     #8b96ac                          {fg.muted}               slate.400
     #64748b #57637c #475569 #3d465a  {fg.muted|0.65 .5 .45 .3} the four dim/disabled greys, as one
                                                                 colour at four alphas (each composite
                                                                 lands within ~4/255 of the legacy hex)
     rgba(100,116,139, ≤0.45)         {border}                 slate-500 wash on panels/tables/dividers
     rgba(100,116,139, ≥0.5)          {border.strong}          the same wash on interactive controls
     rgba(30,41,59, a)                {bg.overlay|a}           navy.800 is (28,39,64): same wash
     rgba(11,18,32, a)                {bg.window|a}            navy.950 is (11,17,32)
     rgba(15,21,34, a)                {bg.surface|a}           navy.900 is (15,23,42)
     rgba(71,85,105,0.5) (#DetailIcon){fg.muted|0.25}          same composite, keeps the plate a wash
     #1e293b  #17233a                 {bg.overlay}             the two popup grounds
     #0b1220 (Daevanion canvas)       {bg.window}              navy.950
     #facc15 #f59e0b #f2a33e #d8a253  {warn} / {warn|0.8}    one amber for gold/estimate/Genius text
     rgba(250,204,21,a) rgba(245,158,11,a)  {warn|a}           the same, as a wash
     rgba(41,32,10,0.4)               {warn|0.12}              a "gold-tinted card" wash, now derived
     #22c55e                          {ok}                     green.400
     #38bdf8 (#SkillTileName)         {accent}                 was Abyss-sky, which is also Legend's
                                                                 grade colour — the tile name is not a grade
     #c084fc (#SlotEnchantLabel)      {accent}                 dead on arrival: app.py overrode this label
                                                                 per theme with ENCHANT_ACCENT_BY_THEME, so
                                                                 the value a user SAW was that table's
                                                                 (#06b6d4 on Abyss).  The table was this
                                                                 app's private copy of "the current theme's
                                                                 accent", so it is gone and the token says it
     rgba(192,132,252,0.18)           {secondary|0.18}         violet.400 wash
     #fb923c #60a5fa #4ade80          {data.role.*}            the three Rolle accents are DATA (MASTER
     rgba(251,146,60,a) &c            {data.role.*|a}          §4-4), owned by core/theme.ROLE_COLORS

   NEAREST-TOKEN MAP, PART 2 — THE MIGRATED INLINE SHEETS.  The map above
   covers this file's hand-written ancestor.  The other 94 sources were
   `setStyleSheet` calls, HTML `<span style=…>` fragments and QPainter
   colours inside ItemDatabase/app.py; review G (M10) pointed out, rightly,
   that they got the same nearest-token treatment with no record.  Here it
   is.  Mappings already listed in PART 1 (the four dim greys, the ambers,
   #e2e8f0/#e6ecf5/#e7ebf3 → {fg}, slate-500 lines → {border}) applied
   identically and are not repeated.

     legacy value                     token                      why
     ------------------------------   ------------------------   ---------------------------------
     #f1f5f9  (3 tooltip titles,      {fg}                       a fourth spelling of "main text"
              1 Arcana card row)
     #a9b7d1  (_DETAIL_CAPTION_       {fg.secondary}             the detail popups' caption grey
              COLOR, 4 HTML spans)
     #aab4c8  (browse-only substat    {fg.secondary}             a boosted-contrast variant of the
              header)                                            same caption (User-reported,
                                                                  2026-09-11: "kaum lesbar")
     #fdfdfd  (Arcana set banner)     {fg}                       near-white painter text
     #f8fafc  (Daevanion hover ring)  {accent.hover}             the lightest accent step, which is
                                                                  what "brighter than active" meant
     #334155  (radio :disabled)       {fg.muted|0.35}            the FIFTH dim grey — PART 1's "four
                                                                  dim greys" line counted the sheet's
                                                                  only, this one was inline
     #0f1b2e  (season button ground)  {bg.elevated}              between navy.900 and navy.850
     #fca5a5  ("not enough points")   {danger}                   red.300 → red.400
     #c084fc  (_ARCANA_WISH_COLOR)    {secondary}                "testweise mal lila" (2026-08-28),
                                                                  i.e. a second accent — which is
                                                                  exactly what `secondary` is
     #06b6d4  (enchant badge, per     {accent}                   see the #SlotEnchantLabel row above
              theme)
     #2dd4bf  (skill-level source     {accent}                   a teal that was Emerald's accent in
              tooltip heading)                                    an Abyss window
     #38bdf8  (2 HTML headings)       {accent}                   same as #SkillTileName above
     rgb(30,41,59)  (HTML table       {bg.elevated}              navy.850; the wash it replaced sat
              ground, 1 tooltip)                                  between .850 and .800
     rgb(56,189,248)  (substat        {accent}                   the "offensive" band was sky, the
              bucket "offensive")                                 accent is cyan (Δ 22,22,10)
     rgb(244,114,182)  (substat       {data.gear_type.PvP}       the "pvp" band was rose, and "PvP"
              bucket "pvp")                                       already means #fb7185 everywhere
                                                                  else in this window (Δ 7,1,49).
                                                                  It was mapped to {secondary} first —
                                                                  a pink→violet shift of Δ(77,25,68),
                                                                  which is what review G caught
     rgb(74,222,128) / rgb(250,204,   {ok} / {warn}              the other two bands, both already
              21)  (the other bands)                              on their token
     QColor(6,10,18,a)  (banner       {bg.window} at a           navy.950 is (11,17,32)
              overlay, 3 stops)
     QColor(71,85,105)  (icon         {border.strong}            slate-600 plate under a missing icon
              placeholder ground)
     QColor(15,22,38,235)  (node      {bg.surface} at 235        navy.900 is (15,23,42)
              tooltip ground)
     QColor(0,0,0,150)  (tooltip      {bg.window} at 150         a black shadow is the window ground
              shadow)                                             on every one of the six themes
     QColor(255,255,255,a)  (banner   {fg} at a                  MASTER §2: never pure white
              border), `color: white`
     #0d9488 / rgba(94,234,212,       data spec_state            kept VERBATIM as a data colour: the
              0.35)  (spec states)                                two values are a user decision about
                                                                  a game mechanic, not a theme choice
     #475569  (icon glow, plate       {border.strong}            the "no grade" fallback ring
              fallback)

   NOT tokenised, on purpose:
     * font-family — nothing.  MASTER's deferred decision "app.setFont() as
       the base-font vehicle, after the Armory wave" is the host's call, and
       retyping 22k lines of layout tuned to the system font is not a
       colour migration.  Font SIZES/WEIGHTS are tokens where a legacy value
       sits exactly on the scale (11/12/13/14/16/20/26 px, 600/700); 9.5,
       10, 10.5, 15, 18, 22, 28 px and `800`/`bold` stay literal.
     * radii, padding, widths — geometry.  This wave changed no metric.
     * `selection-color` on the item views — kept, because the Armory paints
       per-rarity item foregrounds itself and the *selected* row is the one
       place a fixed colour is correct.  `color` on an item view stays
       forbidden (MASTER §4-8). */
QWidget {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: {{text_md}}px;
}

/* Tooltips otherwise render as a plain native OS tooltip (white/black,
   one long unwrapped line) -- User-reported, 2026-08-29, re: the
   Estimated Damage button's tooltip. Matches the app's own dark panel
   look instead. */
QToolTip {
    background-color: {{bg_surface}};
    color: {{fg}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    font-size: {{text_sm}}px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border: 1px solid {{fg_muted|0.6}};
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.75}};
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background-color: {{accent|0.85}};
    border: 1px solid {{accent}};
}

#PageTitle {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: {{text_2xl}}px;
    font-weight: bold;
}

#PageSubtitle {
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
}

#TopBar {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.55}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 10px;
}

QLineEdit {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.75}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 9px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: {{text_md}}px;
}

QLineEdit:focus {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.8}};
}

QComboBox {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.92}};
    color: {{fg}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 30px 8px 12px;
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
    min-height: 20px;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.7}};
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    border: none;
    width: 22px;
}

/* No down-arrow rule existed before -- drop-down reserved 22px of empty
   space but never drew anything into it, so every combo box (Grade/
   Category/Class filter row) rendered as a plain borderless field with no
   visual "this opens a dropdown" affordance. A CSS-only border-triangle
   was tried first but rendered as a solid grey square instead of a
   triangle (Qt's ::down-arrow subcontrol sizing doesn't cooperate with the
   web border-trick) -- using a real small PNG asset instead, same pattern
   as every other bundled image in this app.  ASSET_PATH is substituted
   with an absolute directory path at render time (core.theme's renderer
   does it for both sheets now, in place of this file's own
   __DROPDOWN_ARROW_URL__ marker); absolute, not relative, so the url()
   also resolves from inside the PyInstaller-bundled exe, whose _MEIPASS
   differs run to run. */
QComboBox::down-arrow {
    image: url(ASSET_PATH/assets/ui/dropdown_arrow.png);
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    margin-right: 10px;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: {{bg_surface}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    selection-background-color: {{accent|0.25}};
    selection-color: {{fg}};
    /* No blanket "color" here (removed 2026-08-29, User-reported: Grade/
       Rarity dropdown items showed plain white instead of their per-
       rarity color) -- a QSS color on an item view overrides each
       QStandardItem's own setForeground() unconditionally, the same
       cascade quirk already documented elsewhere this session (Round 20,
       see project_arcana_planner.md). Falls back to the app-wide dark
       QPalette's Text role (#e5e7eb, main.py's _dark_palette) for any
       combo that doesn't color its own items -- visually identical to
       the #e2e8f0 this used to hardcode. */
    padding: 4px;
}

/* Popup list item padding only -- the hover HIGHLIGHT itself is painted in
   Python (_ComboHoverDelegate in app.py), not here: a "::item:hover" QSS
   rule was tried first (User-reported, 2026-09-02) but never took visible
   effect, the same class of "app-wide stylesheet overrides native per-item
   painting" issue _RoleColorDelegate's own docstring already documents for
   per-item text color. */
QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    padding: 4px 8px;
}


#ResultLabel {
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
}

QTableView {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.55}};
    alternate-background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.45}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 10px;
    gridline-color: {{border}};
    color: {{fg}};
    selection-background-color: {{accent|0.25}};
    selection-color: {{fg}};
}

QTableView::item {
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border: none;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.9}};
    color: {{fg_secondary}};
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border: none;
    border-right: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-bottom: 1px solid {{border}};
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    font-size: {{text_sm}}px;
}

QHeaderView::section:hover {
    background-color: {{accent|0.18}};
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: transparent;
    width: 12px;
    margin: 0;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background: {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 6px;
    min-height: 24px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background: {{fg_muted|0.7}};
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    height: 0;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: transparent;
    height: 12px;
    margin: 0;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background: {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 6px;
    min-width: 24px;
}

/* Grade badge colors used in the Grade column via Qt.ForegroundRole per-item,
   kept here only as reference values used directly in app.py:
   Common #94a3b8, Rare #38bdf8, Unique #a855f7, Epic #f59e0b, Legend #facc15 */

QPushButton {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.75}};
    color: {{fg}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 14px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
}

QPushButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.7}};
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: {{accent|0.2}};
}

/* Stat Priority editor's gear icon button (QToolButton, no default styling
   of its own unlike QPushButton above) -- matches the surrounding buttons'
   card look instead of Qt's flat native ToolButton chrome. */
#StatPriorityEditBtn {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.75}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 8px;
}

#StatPriorityEditBtn:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.7}};
}

#StatPriorityEditBtn:pressed {
    background-color: {{accent|0.2}};
}

/* Per-skill level -/+ buttons (Skill Description cards) -- same card look
   as the default QPushButton rule above, just without its 8px/14px padding,
   which would otherwise crush a 26x26 icon-only button down to almost
   nothing. */
#SkillLevelStepBtn {
    padding: 0px;
}

#SkillLevelValue {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    font-size: {{text_md}}px;
}

/* Arcana wish -/+ counter (User-Wunsch, 2026-08-28/29) -- same icon-only
   sizing fix as #SkillLevelStepBtn, plus a subtle purple hover so it reads
   as a distinct, secondary control from the main level counter above it. */
#ArcanaWishStepBtn {
    padding: 0px;
    border-radius: 10px;
}

#ArcanaWishStepBtn:hover {
    background-color: {{secondary|0.18}};
}

#DetailIcon {
    background-color: {{fg_muted|0.25}};
    border: 1px solid {{fg_muted|0.4}};
    border-radius: 12px;
}

#DetailName {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    font-size: {{text_md}}px;
}

#DetailHeader {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
}

#GearScoreHeaderLabel {
    color: {{accent}};
    font-size: {{text_xl}}px;
    font-weight: 800;
}

#DetailInfo {
    color: {{fg_secondary}};
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
}

/* Substat card value, right-aligned opposite its #DetailInfo label (User-
   approved mockup, 2026-09-11) -- browse-only Item Database popup only. */
#DetailInfoValue {
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
}

/* Header-band / body divider in the redesigned browse-only gear popup. */
#DetailHeaderDivider {
    background-color: {{border}};
    max-height: 1px;
    border: none;
}

#DetailEnchantValue {
    color: {{warn}};
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    font-size: {{text_md}}px;
}

#EquipPriorityArrow {
    color: {{accent}};
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 28px;
}

#ChainNode {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 9px;
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: 9.5px;
    padding: 4px;
}
#ChainNode:hover:enabled {
    background: {{fg_muted|0.08}};
}
#ChainNode[expanded="true"] {
    background: {{accent|0.14}};
    border-color: {{accent|0.4}};
}
#ChainNode:disabled {
    color: {{fg_muted|0.65}};
}

#ExpandableMaterialHeader {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: {{fg}};
    font-size: {{text_base}}px;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 4px 0;
}
#ExpandableMaterialHeader:hover {
    color: {{accent}};
}
#ExpandableMaterialHeader[expanded="true"] {
    color: {{accent}};
}

#ChainArrow {
    color: {{accent}};
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    font-size: 15px;
    padding-top: 14px;
}

#ChainSidePanel {
    background: {{bg_surface|0.6}};
    border: 1px solid {{fg_muted|0.14}};
    border-radius: 8px;
}

#ChainSideLabel {
    color: {{accent}};
    font-size: 10.5px;
}

#DetailDisclaimer {
    color: {{warn}};
    font-size: {{text_xs}}px;
    font-style: italic;
}

#SlotIconButton {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.75}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
    padding: 4px;
}

#SlotIconButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.8}};
    background-color: {{accent|0.1}};
}

#SlotIconButton:pressed {
    background-color: {{accent|0.25}};
}

/* Pantheon board (User-Wunsch, 2026-09-04) -- radially-positioned slots
   drawn straight onto #PantheonCanvas (no layout manager, see
   _build_pantheon_tab), so this panel needs its own explicit dark
   background rather than inheriting one from a layout container. Artwork
   keeps #SlotIconButton's rounded-rect look; Statue/Colossus get a real
   circular radius (half their own fixed size) to match the sketch, with
   Colossus additionally gold-accented since it's the board's centerpiece. */
#PantheonCanvas {
    background-color: {{bg_window|0.55}};
    border: 1px solid {{fg_muted|0.14}};
    border-radius: 16px;
}

#PantheonArtworkSlot,
#PantheonStatueSlot,
#PantheonColossusSlot {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.85}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    color: {{fg_muted}};
}

#PantheonArtworkSlot {
    border-radius: 12px;
}

#PantheonStatueSlot {
    border-radius: 33px;
}

#PantheonColossusSlot {
    border-radius: 54px;
    border: 2px solid {{warn|0.55}};
}

#PantheonArtworkSlot:hover,
#PantheonStatueSlot:hover {
    border-color: {{accent|0.8}};
    background-color: {{accent|0.1}};
}

#PantheonColossusSlot:hover {
    border-color: {{warn|0.9}};
    background-color: {{warn|0.12}};
}

#PantheonArtworkSlot:pressed,
#PantheonStatueSlot:pressed {
    background-color: {{accent|0.25}};
}

#PantheonColossusSlot:pressed {
    background-color: {{warn|0.25}};
}

/* "Active" slot -- the one the left inventory panel is currently assigning
   into (User-Wunsch, 2026-09-05, replacing the per-slot popup picker).
   Set via a dynamic property (see _on_pantheon_slot_clicked), not :checked,
   since QToolButton here isn't checkable -- only ever one slot at a time. */
#PantheonArtworkSlot[pantheonActive="true"],
#PantheonStatueSlot[pantheonActive="true"] {
    border: 2px solid {{accent}};
    background-color: {{accent|0.22}};
}

#PantheonColossusSlot[pantheonActive="true"] {
    border: 2px solid {{warn}};
    background-color: {{warn|0.22}};
}

#SlotEnchantLabel {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: {{accent}};
    font-size: {{text_xs}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    padding: 1px;
}

#EquipSectionLabel {
    color: {{accent}};
    font-size: {{text_xs}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    letter-spacing: 1px;
}

#SkillFilterButton {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.6}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: {{text_sm}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
    padding: 4px 10px;
}

#SkillFilterButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.6}};
    color: {{fg}};
}

#SkillFilterButton:checked {
    background-color: {{accent|0.22}};
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.9}};
    color: {{accent}};
}

/* "Estimated Damage" toggle -- same base look as SkillFilterButton, but
   with the damage-number orange accent (User-Wunsch, 2026-08-29: "leicht
   von den anderen Filtern abheben ... leicht orange faerben") so it reads
   as a different KIND of toggle (an estimate, not a filter) rather than
   blending into the Favorites/Checked-only pills next to it. Own
   #-scoped rule, not #SkillFilterButton directly, so this doesn't affect
   any other SkillFilterButton in the app. */
#SkillEstimatedDamageButton {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.6}};
    border: 1px solid {{warn|0.35}};
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: {{warn|0.8}};
    font-size: {{text_sm}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
    padding: 4px 10px;
}

#SkillEstimatedDamageButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{warn|0.7}};
    color: {{warn}};
}

#SkillEstimatedDamageButton:checked {
    background-color: {{warn|0.2}};
    border: 1px solid {{warn|0.9}};
    color: {{warn}};
}

/* "EQ Priority" button, bottom-right of the Jewelry column -- same base
   look as SkillFilterButton but bigger font/padding since the plain
   12px/4-10px version still read as too small/easy to miss there
   (User-Wunsch, 2026-08-27: "der Button unten Rechts wird sonst
   übersehen ... einen längeren Button ... Schriftgröße anpassen"). Own
   #-scoped rule, not #SkillFilterButton directly, so this doesn't affect
   any other SkillFilterButton in the app. */
#EqPriorityButton {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.6}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 9px;
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_bold}};
    padding: 8px 20px;
}

#EqPriorityButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.6}};
    color: {{fg}};
}

/* Back-arrow/X pair on a full-panel takeover page (EQ Priority, and reused
   by any future one) -- plain QToolButtons had no styling at all before
   this, just bare native icon chrome (User-Wunsch, 2026-08-28: "den
   Backpfeil und das 'X' an den Stil anpassen"). Same dark-card/cyan-hover
   language as #SlotIconButton, just round for a 32px icon button instead
   of square for a slot tile. */
#PanelNavButton {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.75}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 16px;
}

#PanelNavButton:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{accent|0.8}};
    background-color: {{accent|0.1}};
}

#PanelNavButton:pressed {
    background-color: {{accent|0.25}};
}

/* Small "x" overlay badge on a filled Skill Priority List slot (User-Wunsch,
   2026-08-28: "die Möglichkeit ... Skills zu entfernen"). */
#PrioritySlotRemoveBtn {
    background-color: {{bg_surface|0.85}};
    border: 1px solid {{border_strong}};
    border-radius: 9px;
}

#PrioritySlotRemoveBtn:hover {
    border: 1px solid {{danger|0.8}};
    background-color: {{danger|0.2}};
}

/* Eigenschaften-Priorität Rolle buttons -- same base look as
   SkillFilterButton, but each role gets its own accent color when checked
   (User-Wunsch: "Angreifer 'Orange', Verteidiger 'Blau' und Support
   'Grün'... bei Auswahl des Reiters eine entsprechende Farbkombi"). Own
   #-scoped rules instead of reusing #SkillFilterButton so this doesn't
   affect any other SkillFilterButton in the app. */
#RoleButtonAngreifer, #RoleButtonVerteidiger, #RoleButtonSupport {
    background-color: {{bg_overlay|0.6}};
    border: 1px solid {{border}};
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: {{fg_muted}};
    font-size: {{text_sm}}px;
    font-weight: {{font_weight_semibold}};
    padding: 4px 10px;
}

#RoleButtonAngreifer:hover { border: 1px solid {{data.role.Angreifer|0.6}}; color: {{fg}}; }
#RoleButtonVerteidiger:hover { border: 1px solid {{data.role.Verteidiger|0.6}}; color: {{fg}}; }
#RoleButtonSupport:hover { border: 1px solid {{data.role.Support|0.6}}; color: {{fg}}; }

#RoleButtonAngreifer:checked {
    background-color: {{data.role.Angreifer|0.22}};
    border: 1px solid {{data.role.Angreifer|0.9}};
    color: {{data.role.Angreifer}};
}
#RoleButtonVerteidiger:checked {
    background-color: {{data.role.Verteidiger|0.22}};
    border: 1px solid {{data.role.Verteidiger|0.9}};
    color: {{data.role.Verteidiger}};
}
#RoleButtonSupport:checked {
    background-color: {{data.role.Support|0.22}};
    border: 1px solid {{data.role.Support|0.9}};
    color: {{data.role.Support}};
}

